(2588134, 355471, 56978, '<td valign="top">very nice and crisp</td>', 'very nice and crisp', '2006-07-05 14:27:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2588137, 356796, 38032, '<td valign="top">The lighting is out of this world, the hair is excellent as well as the skin.  The complementary colors are great ... Not seeing the mouth due to a flower being stuffed there just kills this for me ... I get it, I think ... but visually it just doesn''t help it. I want to like it more than I do ... technically perfect, but doesn''t have great appeal to me overall ... I''m sure if the flower wern''t there you''d have people saying that the focus wasn''t on the flowers.</td>', 'The lighting is out of this world, the hair is excellent as well as the skin.  The complementary colors are great ... Not seeing the mouth due to a flower being stuffed there just kills this for me ... I get it, I think ... but visually it just doesn''t help it. I want to like it more than I do ... technically perfect, but doesn''t have great appeal to me overall ... I''m sure if the flower wern''t there you''d have people saying that the focus wasn''t on the flowers.', '2006-07-05 14:27:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2588140, 355679, 22288, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, the flower just seems a bit overpowering in its saturation. 6</td>', 'I like the idea, the flower just seems a bit overpowering in its saturation. 6', '2006-07-05 14:28:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2588146, 356909, 5112, '<td valign="top">Beautiful callas, well photographed (although the image is a bit dark IMO).  What I''m not so sure of is the concept.  The placement of the flowers seems so artificial, and without any apparent purpose. (6)<br/> <br/>Looking at it again :)<br/> <br/>The light on the flowers is really quite beautiful, especially the two laying down flowers.  Now I''m thinking "tic-tac-toe".  These things are really hard to photograph.  I better quit while I''m behind.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-05 14:42:56.</i></td>', 'Beautiful callas, well photographed (although the image is a bit dark IMO).  What I''m not so sure of is the concept.  The placement of the flowers seems so artificial, and without any apparent purpose. (6) Looking at it again :) The light on the flowers is really quite beautiful, especially the two laying down flowers.  Now I''m thinking "tic-tac-toe".  These things are really hard to photograph.  I better quit while I''m behind.', '2006-07-05 14:29:47.000000', '2006-07-05 15:42:56.000000', 1),
(2588147, 356715, 5112, '<td valign="top">Looking at the sunset through a hole in the grasses or flowers?   Beautiful idea, although I don''t think it works quite right here.  Maybe the "frame" is too busy (in particular the x like silhouette is distracting)?  I don''t know.  I think it''s a concept that''s worthy of a lot more exploration, but as it is it doesn''t quite look right.  (6)</td>', 'Looking at the sunset through a hole in the grasses or flowers?   Beautiful idea, although I don''t think it works quite right here.  Maybe the "frame" is too busy (in particular the x like silhouette is distracting)?  I don''t know.  I think it''s a concept that''s worthy of a lot more exploration, but as it is it doesn''t quite look right.  (6)', '2006-07-05 14:30:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2588156, 355215, 22288, '<td valign="top">Very Nice 9</td>', 'Very Nice 9', '2006-07-05 14:32:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2588163, 354701, 22288, '<td valign="top">Cute idea, good color, I especially like how crisp the picture feels. 8</td>', 'Cute idea, good color, I especially like how crisp the picture feels. 8', '2006-07-05 14:33:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2588166, 356175, 22288, '<td valign="top">I like how the picture draws you right to the subject. Nice Shot. 8</td>', 'I like how the picture draws you right to the subject. Nice Shot. 8', '2006-07-05 14:34:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2588168, 355839, 56978, '<td valign="top">nice and sharp but doesn''t look like you''re using the full 640 pixels...</td>', 'nice and sharp but doesn''t look like you''re using the full 640 pixels...', '2006-07-05 14:34:49.000000', NULL, 1),
