(2607363, 353994, 16241, '<td valign="top">congratulations ursula, title fits perfectly!</td>', 'congratulations ursula, title fits perfectly!', '2006-07-10 14:27:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607371, 356843, 42792, '<td valign="top">Had hoped to see this place much higher (gave it a 9).  It''s rather haunting and draws in the viewer IMO.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Had hoped to see this place much higher (gave it a 9).  It''s rather haunting and draws in the viewer IMO.  Keep up the good work.', '2006-07-10 14:29:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607374, 353994, 45524, '<td valign="top">What a stunning image you have made here. I didnt get to vote on it, but I can assure you it would have given you another 10. The colors the DOF and the angle make this shot worthy of the ribbon. I dont think I would change a thing, of course that would mean I could make the shot look like you did(highly unlikely). Very well done and congrats on yet another Ribbon.</td>', 'What a stunning image you have made here. I didnt get to vote on it, but I can assure you it would have given you another 10. The colors the DOF and the angle make this shot worthy of the ribbon. I dont think I would change a thing, of course that would mean I could make the shot look like you did(highly unlikely). Very well done and congrats on yet another Ribbon.', '2006-07-10 14:29:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607382, 356253, 40718, '<td valign="top">Well, at the very least it''s creative, eh?  I do wonder a tiny bit about the subject.  Is this usual to take a bath with flowers?  I saw all the rose petals in the tub in American Beauty, but this is a bit different. ;)<br/> <br/>But going with the shot, a few things.  First, could you have actually reversed yourself in the tub and shot with your foot on the other end?  That would remove the drain.  I think it''s an extraneous element and distracts.  Removing as many unnecessary elements as possible is always a good thing in my mind. (With that in mind, the pink container in the background might qualify as well.  I didn''t find that nearly as bad though.)<br/> <br/>I like the polish.  But I guess that''s my personal taste. ;)  Here''s a trick you can try.  Use "Filter&gt;Noise&gt;Dust and scratches at a very low setting to try to remove some of those tiny highlights.  Sometimes things can look a lot better after that.  It''s even basic legal (in case you need it for those challenges).</td>', 'Well, at the very least it''s creative, eh?  I do wonder a tiny bit about the subject.  Is this usual to take a bath with flowers?  I saw all the rose petals in the tub in American Beauty, but this is a bit different. ;) But going with the shot, a few things.  First, could you have actually reversed yourself in the tub and shot with your foot on the other end?  That would remove the drain.  I think it''s an extraneous element and distracts.  Removing as many unnecessary elements as possible is always a good thing in my mind. (With that in mind, the pink container in the background might qualify as well.  I didn''t find that nearly as bad though.) I like the polish.  But I guess that''s my personal taste. ;)  Here''s a trick you can try.  Use "Filter>Noise>Dust and scratches at a very low setting to try to remove some of those tiny highlights.  Sometimes things can look a lot better after that.  It''s even basic legal (in case you need it for those challenges).', '2006-07-10 14:32:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607397, 356131, 19035, '<td valign="top">I was one of your 9 votes, I think its so sad that people cant think out of the box when voting and at least vote also on technical merit, your composition, originality and lighting alone warranted a much higher score than the people that gave you 1''s, 2''s and 3''s.  Take solice in knowing that you worked hard on this and came up with a very wonderful photo.  Job well done, regardless of your score.</td>', 'I was one of your 9 votes, I think its so sad that people cant think out of the box when voting and at least vote also on technical merit, your composition, originality and lighting alone warranted a much higher score than the people that gave you 1''s, 2''s and 3''s.  Take solice in knowing that you worked hard on this and came up with a very wonderful photo.  Job well done, regardless of your score.', '2006-07-10 14:36:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607425, 357141, 30861, '<td valign="top">Shockingly low finish on a serene and compelling image. You had a high vote from me :-)</td>', 'Shockingly low finish on a serene and compelling image. You had a high vote from me :-)', '2006-07-10 14:45:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607426, 356131, 34659, '<td valign="top">I was also one of your 9 votes.  LOVE the creativity here.  There are just a couple of nitpicky technical issues with the shot, but otherwise I thought it was great.  Very underrated IMHO.  Nice work!  :-)</td>', 'I was also one of your 9 votes.  LOVE the creativity here.  There are just a couple of nitpicky technical issues with the shot, but otherwise I thought it was great.  Very underrated IMHO.  Nice work!  :-)', '2006-07-10 14:45:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607427, 356820, 40718, '<td valign="top">Ha, my first thought was "how the hell is this qualifying as 4.5-5.5?"  but I see you just made it in.<br/> <br/>It''s a quality photo.  I think that can be noted by the average commenter vote of 7.28.  Those that took more than 3-5 seconds on the picture appreciated it.  I bet the largest factor was simply voter fatigue.  Look at all those 5''s...<br/> <br/>I have very little to say about this photo because I like it.  I would have given it a 7.  Likely not higher because it does lack that "holy cow" factor.  That doesn''t mean it''s bad at all; I''ve got lots of shots I like a lot that don''t have that, but "holy cow" (otherwise known as "wow") does rule here on DPC.<br/> <br/>Don''t change anything.  OK, clone out those two tiny dots on the front petal.  There.  Nicely done.  Should have been a 6+ for sure.  Come on! Ursula gave it an 8, what more do you need?</td>', 'Ha, my first thought was "how the hell is this qualifying as 4.5-5.5?"  but I see you just made it in. It''s a quality photo.  I think that can be noted by the average commenter vote of 7.28.  Those that took more than 3-5 seconds on the picture appreciated it.  I bet the largest factor was simply voter fatigue.  Look at all those 5''s... I have very little to say about this photo because I like it.  I would have given it a 7.  Likely not higher because it does lack that "holy cow" factor.  That doesn''t mean it''s bad at all; I''ve got lots of shots I like a lot that don''t have that, but "holy cow" (otherwise known as "wow") does rule here on DPC. Don''t change anything.  OK, clone out those two tiny dots on the front petal.  There.  Nicely done.  Should have been a 6+ for sure.  Come on! Ursula gave it an 8, what more do you need?', '2006-07-10 14:46:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607442, 356131, 38127, '<td valign="top">Totally reminds me of the lips from the rocky horror picture show... and that my friend is a Good thing...<br/>I think this is brilliant and it is nice to see that level of creativity. You''re right its way out of the box ..but kudo''s to you for doing it. I didnt vote but you would have scored high from me. <br/>~R~</td>', 'Totally reminds me of the lips from the rocky horror picture show... and that my friend is a Good thing...I think this is brilliant and it is nice to see that level of creativity. You''re right its way out of the box ..but kudo''s to you for doing it. I didnt vote but you would have scored high from me. ~R~', '2006-07-10 14:49:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607444, 354085, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oh Dawn!  You did a GREAT job on this!  I love this photo!  The lighting is so beautiful.   I envy the ability to get that kind of lighting in photos!!!<br/> <br/>I have to admit being in shock that this one is in 61st place????????  No way!!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh Dawn!  You did a GREAT job on this!  I love this photo!  The lighting is so beautiful.   I envy the ability to get that kind of lighting in photos!!! I have to admit being in shock that this one is in 61st place????????  No way!!! ', '2006-07-10 14:51:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2607448, 357155, 24454, '<td valign="top">This is AWESOME!!!  And what a cute title!  The vibrant colors and perfect depth of field make this such a happy photo  :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is AWESOME!!!  And what a cute title!  The vibrant colors and perfect depth of field make this such a happy photo  :) ', '2006-07-10 14:52:13.000000', NULL, 0),
