(2608031, 356715, 55330, '<td valign="top">Made this a favorite</td>', 'Made this a favorite', '2006-07-10 18:00:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608074, 356495, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 5.  I know how difficult it is to photograph crepe myrtles - a tripod is likely the only way unless you get very good lighting as well.  The color seems true to me and not oversaturated, although the line is <i>very</i> thin on in-camera color reproduction.  The tips given by Dr Achoo are very helpful there.  Again, difficult to photograph the color with these flowers.  If this were sharper and a variation in composition to give more overall balance and allow for a better ''study'' of this beautiful flower, make this even better in my opinion.<i>edit:typo</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-10 17:22:42.</i></td>', 'I gave this a 5.  I know how difficult it is to photograph crepe myrtles - a tripod is likely the only way unless you get very good lighting as well.  The color seems true to me and not oversaturated, although the line is very thin on in-camera color reproduction.  The tips given by Dr Achoo are very helpful there.  Again, difficult to photograph the color with these flowers.  If this were sharper and a variation in composition to give more overall balance and allow for a better ''study'' of this beautiful flower, make this even better in my opinion.edit:typo', '2006-07-10 18:20:31.000000', '2006-07-10 18:22:42.000000', 0),
(2608080, 355346, 7889, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments/votes<br/> <br/>Mike<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all your comments/votes Mike', '2006-07-10 18:21:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608121, 356796, 22872, '<td valign="top">I would love to see this made into a black and white with the flowers painted back in as a light yellow?  and maybe her eyes barely painted back as a light blue?  might turn out cool... :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'I would love to see this made into a black and white with the flowers painted back in as a light yellow?  and maybe her eyes barely painted back as a light blue?  might turn out cool... :) ', '2006-07-10 18:29:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608143, 353994, 39850, '<td valign="top">''Phew'', glad I was right (<i>although there was another entry dangerously close to your style)</i>, but my money was on this.  Beautiful abstract and colors, as usual.  Congratulations.</td>', '''Phew'', glad I was right (although there was another entry dangerously close to your style), but my money was on this.  Beautiful abstract and colors, as usual.  Congratulations.', '2006-07-10 18:34:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608156, 357186, 39850, '<td valign="top">Fooled me with that silk flower - guess I was so ''taken'' with the capture <i>(set-up or not)</i>, that despite wanting more detail in the flower <i>(and I now know why there isn''t)</i>, I obviously didn''t ''inspect'' it very well.  Creative, as usual.  Nice use of a peanut.  Congratulations.</td>', 'Fooled me with that silk flower - guess I was so ''taken'' with the capture (set-up or not), that despite wanting more detail in the flower (and I now know why there isn''t), I obviously didn''t ''inspect'' it very well.  Creative, as usual.  Nice use of a peanut.  Congratulations.', '2006-07-10 18:35:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608168, 357323, 25397, '<td valign="top">You owe me a chocolate bar. <br/> <br/>I like it though</td>', 'You owe me a chocolate bar.  I like it though', '2006-07-10 18:37:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608180, 355816, 25397, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by goodman:</b></div><hr/><i> perfect editing, have no idea why this didnt score higher! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Same here, weird!<br/> <br/>Love ya Larus ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by goodman: perfect editing, have no idea why this didnt score higher!  Same here, weird! Love ya Larus ;-)', '2006-07-10 18:39:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608259, 355730, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Excellent bokeh and a pretty good closeup of the bee.  What I like is how the size of the bee emphasizes the petite nature and delicateness of the flower''s blossoms.  I gave this a 6 in voting.  I suspect this was shot in full sunshine, which makes it tough to get good contrast across the spectrum, though the color of the flower itself is very good.</td>', 'Trading Post comment Excellent bokeh and a pretty good closeup of the bee.  What I like is how the size of the bee emphasizes the petite nature and delicateness of the flower''s blossoms.  I gave this a 6 in voting.  I suspect this was shot in full sunshine, which makes it tough to get good contrast across the spectrum, though the color of the flower itself is very good.', '2006-07-10 18:59:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608288, 356359, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>I gave this a 6 because by gosh, it wasn''t just another flower!  I thought it fit for a flower challenge around the 4th of July just fine, but then I''m weird.  I kinda like the long horizontal crop, too.  I suspect a lot of the scoring is either DNMC related or crop related.</td>', 'Trading Post comment I gave this a 6 because by gosh, it wasn''t just another flower!  I thought it fit for a flower challenge around the 4th of July just fine, but then I''m weird.  I kinda like the long horizontal crop, too.  I suspect a lot of the scoring is either DNMC related or crop related.', '2006-07-10 19:08:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608307, 357186, 46999, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo on nearly all levels, and it is a perfect example of when manipulation of a scene before and after capture is appropriate.  The best thing about this photo, and its accompanying story, is that it is a fantastic example of seeing an image in your mind and then working overtime to capture it in your camera.</td>', 'This is a great photo on nearly all levels, and it is a perfect example of when manipulation of a scene before and after capture is appropriate.  The best thing about this photo, and its accompanying story, is that it is a fantastic example of seeing an image in your mind and then working overtime to capture it in your camera.', '2006-07-10 19:11:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608331, 356395, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>At the risk of repeating myself, I really do like this composition - the almost-touching shape formed the branch and its reflection is quite lovely.  Colors work well, too.  About the only thing I''d recommend is try playing with levels a bit to see if you can get the white more white, and if you still like it that way.  You can also try "selective color" and take the yellow and a bit of the magenta and cyan out of the white.</td>', 'Trading Post comment At the risk of repeating myself, I really do like this composition - the almost-touching shape formed the branch and its reflection is quite lovely.  Colors work well, too.  About the only thing I''d recommend is try playing with levels a bit to see if you can get the white more white, and if you still like it that way.  You can also try "selective color" and take the yellow and a bit of the magenta and cyan out of the white.', '2006-07-10 19:19:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608337, 353994, 2178, '<td valign="top">my goodness thats gorgeous, congrats!</td>', 'my goodness thats gorgeous, congrats!', '2006-07-10 19:21:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608347, 353994, 6597, '<td valign="top">Congrats on another ribbon and beautiful photo a well desired ribbon<br/>               Sue</td>', 'Congrats on another ribbon and beautiful photo a well desired ribbon               Sue', '2006-07-10 19:22:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608351, 355861, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Good to see a submission from you - it''s been awhile!  And congrats on a new picture in your top row.<br/> <br/>I gave this a 7 in voting.  It''s a lovely, simple, captivating image and I really like the depth and texture of the flower itself.  I also like the way the glass vase appears, with the water line echoing the table line below.  Like the tonality and shading of the background as well.  My only quibble is the solid, featureless appearance of the leaves.  They don''t need to be detailed, and for all I know Mapplethorpe''s leaves all look this way, but the barest hint of shape and surface might be kinda nice.</td>', 'Trading Post comment Good to see a submission from you - it''s been awhile!  And congrats on a new picture in your top row. I gave this a 7 in voting.  It''s a lovely, simple, captivating image and I really like the depth and texture of the flower itself.  I also like the way the glass vase appears, with the water line echoing the table line below.  Like the tonality and shading of the background as well.  My only quibble is the solid, featureless appearance of the leaves.  They don''t need to be detailed, and for all I know Mapplethorpe''s leaves all look this way, but the barest hint of shape and surface might be kinda nice.', '2006-07-10 19:23:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608377, 356072, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comments<br/> <br/>I thought you entered "StationEry"?  And since you''ll probably ribbon with it, I won''t have many comments other than "Congrats" on that one anyway...  :-)<br/> <br/>I actually kinda liked this, since it was more of an "in context" kinda shot.  Think it should have been about a 5.5 on the DPC-scale, but when there were so many amazing close-ups, I can see how this one probably got passed over.  A bit tighter crop to lose the bench in the back might help just a tad.</td>', 'Trading Post comments I thought you entered "StationEry"?  And since you''ll probably ribbon with it, I won''t have many comments other than "Congrats" on that one anyway...  :-) I actually kinda liked this, since it was more of an "in context" kinda shot.  Think it should have been about a 5.5 on the DPC-scale, but when there were so many amazing close-ups, I can see how this one probably got passed over.  A bit tighter crop to lose the bench in the back might help just a tad.', '2006-07-10 19:30:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608391, 355397, 30982, '<td valign="top">This was one of six 9s I gave out in this challenge (and I gave no 10s - I''m skimpy on 10s).  I really like the zen-like quality and peacefulness of this shot.  Very well done and unfortunately underrated (but not underappreciated!)</td>', 'This was one of six 9s I gave out in this challenge (and I gave no 10s - I''m skimpy on 10s).  I really like the zen-like quality and peacefulness of this shot.  Very well done and unfortunately underrated (but not underappreciated!)', '2006-07-10 19:34:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608468, 357064, 32997, '<td valign="top">The tones are amazing..what a wonderful bit of processing. Great work.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-10 22:12:31.</i></td>', 'The tones are amazing..what a wonderful bit of processing. Great work.', '2006-07-10 19:57:22.000000', '2006-07-10 23:12:31.000000', 0),
(2608476, 357123, 42567, '<td valign="top">Great picture!  Congratulations on your top 20.</td>', 'Great picture!  Congratulations on your top 20.', '2006-07-10 20:00:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608561, 353891, 1717, '<td valign="top">well, i think it''s absolutely beautiful!  there aren''t many things i like more than flowers photographed in this way.  it has such a sad and fragile mood even more enhanced by the drops of rain.  this should have finished much, much higher!<br/> <br/>thank you for the tribute, Robert.  i am truly honored with such a lovely photo.<br/> <br/>hugs</td>', 'well, i think it''s absolutely beautiful!  there aren''t many things i like more than flowers photographed in this way.  it has such a sad and fragile mood even more enhanced by the drops of rain.  this should have finished much, much higher! thank you for the tribute, Robert.  i am truly honored with such a lovely photo. hugs', '2006-07-10 20:38:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608562, 357130, 49652, '<td valign="top">This was underrated in my opinion.  I loved it.</td>', 'This was underrated in my opinion.  I loved it.', '2006-07-10 20:39:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608574, 356376, 14476, '<td valign="top">I did the best I could with this image in the scoring.  It is excellent, with fine placement on the page, superior lighting and excellent subject matter.  You had strong competition which must have been the only reason this isn''t in the top three.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'I did the best I could with this image in the scoring.  It is excellent, with fine placement on the page, superior lighting and excellent subject matter.  You had strong competition which must have been the only reason this isn''t in the top three. Keep up the good work. Alice', '2006-07-10 20:42:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2608636, 353994, 55330, '<td valign="top">Congrats</td>', 'Congrats', '2006-07-10 21:04:17.000000', NULL, 0),
