(2624485, 357246, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Patrinus, hello!  You have a nice image here that certainly scored comparatively well in this tremendous field of terrific flower pics.<br/> <br/>Nice composition, and lovely colors, of course.<br/> <br/>Since it is the mission of the Critique Club to suggest ways to make your image ''better'' I''ll do my best.  <br/> <br/>I would suggest first that the image gives the appearance of being slightly oversharpened.  At least the charactaristic haloing shows up on my screen.  Some of our more technically oriented voters may have noted that.  <br/> <br/>The other is a personal opinion.  I wonder if a different cropping would change this very nice image to make it more appealing.  I put your orchid in different spots on my monitor, and really liked it when just the wings and that great red center were showing, eliminating most of the lower half of the picture.  Again, just a thought.<br/> <br/>It''s always nice to come across your work, and I''m pleased to have had the opportunity to enjoy this one again.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Patrinus, hello!  You have a nice image here that certainly scored comparatively well in this tremendous field of terrific flower pics. Nice composition, and lovely colors, of course. Since it is the mission of the Critique Club to suggest ways to make your image ''better'' I''ll do my best.   I would suggest first that the image gives the appearance of being slightly oversharpened.  At least the charactaristic haloing shows up on my screen.  Some of our more technically oriented voters may have noted that.   The other is a personal opinion.  I wonder if a different cropping would change this very nice image to make it more appealing.  I put your orchid in different spots on my monitor, and really liked it when just the wings and that great red center were showing, eliminating most of the lower half of the picture.  Again, just a thought. It''s always nice to come across your work, and I''m pleased to have had the opportunity to enjoy this one again. Alice', '2006-07-15 11:20:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2624584, 356783, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Hello!  Congratulations on your nice placement in the Flower challenge.  This is, of course, a striking image, and immediately engendered strong emotions from your commentors.  <br/> <br/>Technically, and compositionally, in my opinion, it''s just fine.  sure it''s bold and the colors almost hurt, but that''s what you wanted and that''s what you achieved.  I very much like the way you made the stems cross on the two lilies.  That added an extra thoughtful touch to the image.  <br/> <br/>I will point out that the lighting on the lavender background is very slightly uneven (but you knew that) and the flowers have a slight indication of oversharpening, at least on my monitor.  But those are pickings of nits, and just something to do to keep my fingers occupied while on the keyboard.<br/> <br/>In any event,  nice image, and I''m very pleased to have the chance to examine it more closely.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Hello!  Congratulations on your nice placement in the Flower challenge.  This is, of course, a striking image, and immediately engendered strong emotions from your commentors.   Technically, and compositionally, in my opinion, it''s just fine.  sure it''s bold and the colors almost hurt, but that''s what you wanted and that''s what you achieved.  I very much like the way you made the stems cross on the two lilies.  That added an extra thoughtful touch to the image.   I will point out that the lighting on the lavender background is very slightly uneven (but you knew that) and the flowers have a slight indication of oversharpening, at least on my monitor.  But those are pickings of nits, and just something to do to keep my fingers occupied while on the keyboard. In any event,  nice image, and I''m very pleased to have the chance to examine it more closely. Keep up the good work. Alice', '2006-07-15 12:40:25.000000', NULL, 0),
