(2625590, 355062, 20530, '<td valign="top">Nice work. Great focus. The flowers really stand out against the BG (great contrast). The composition is very nice; although I''m compelled (as a former floral designer and artist) to suggest that an odd number of flowers would be better. Since the colors of vase and flowers are in different families, I converted this to B/W and cloned out the rose. I think it looks stunning that way, too.<br/> <br/>Cool vase. Look forward to seeing you use it again.</td>', 'Nice work. Great focus. The flowers really stand out against the BG (great contrast). The composition is very nice; although I''m compelled (as a former floral designer and artist) to suggest that an odd number of flowers would be better. Since the colors of vase and flowers are in different families, I converted this to B/W and cloned out the rose. I think it looks stunning that way, too. Cool vase. Look forward to seeing you use it again.', '2006-07-15 22:06:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2625860, 355958, 11793, '<td valign="top">Nice !<br/> <br/></td>', 'Nice ! ', '2006-07-16 00:30:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2625863, 357238, 17148, '<td valign="top">:: Critique Club :: <br/> <br/>First off this is a pretty shot of flowers and the color is very nice. The thing I think hurt this shot is it is a very average point and click shot of flowers. Try to go for a bit of a different angle next timejust experiment. Dont want to tell you that it would look better up-close or down lowjust find something that looks good to you and that makes an ordinary flower shot stand out a bit more than others. Alsonot surebut you might want to watch your highlightslooks as if they might barely be going and leaving with the texture that use to be there. See it on the whitest parts of the flowers. Like I saidyour shot is not a bad onebut the score you got fit your image for this challenge.it is pretty but so were almost all the other flowershave to find that little something that makes people stop that extra second or two on yours and gives a point or so higher.<br/></td>', ':: Critique Club ::  First off this is a pretty shot of flowers and the color is very nice. The thing I think hurt this shot is it is a very average point and click shot of flowers. Try to go for a bit of a different angle next timejust experiment. Dont want to tell you that it would look better up-close or down lowjust find something that looks good to you and that makes an ordinary flower shot stand out a bit more than others. Alsonot surebut you might want to watch your highlightslooks as if they might barely be going and leaving with the texture that use to be there. See it on the whitest parts of the flowers. Like I saidyour shot is not a bad onebut the score you got fit your image for this challenge.it is pretty but so were almost all the other flowershave to find that little something that makes people stop that extra second or two on yours and gives a point or so higher.', '2006-07-16 00:30:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2626005, 356123, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC.  Wow Joey, nice change of pace for you! You are so talented.  What I like about this image is the mood that you are conveying.  What really is what you do successfully in all the shots I have seen of yours.  The subtle light, color and fog here all make a dreamy and beautiful sultry image.  I like that the glistening light on the flower tips is also on the edge of the shore, makes for a good continuity  in the image.<br/>Excellent use of the foreground, nice compostion.  Excellent job again, Kudos!<br/> <br/>Lynn</td>', 'Greetings from the CC.  Wow Joey, nice change of pace for you! You are so talented.  What I like about this image is the mood that you are conveying.  What really is what you do successfully in all the shots I have seen of yours.  The subtle light, color and fog here all make a dreamy and beautiful sultry image.  I like that the glistening light on the flower tips is also on the edge of the shore, makes for a good continuity  in the image.Excellent use of the foreground, nice compostion.  Excellent job again, Kudos! Lynn', '2006-07-16 01:41:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2626012, 357123, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC!<br/>Very nice job, no distracting elements, good light and colors. <br/>What I like most is your choice of composition is good but my favorite is what you chose as the '' most in focus''  this is not the typical focal point but with all the other very well chosen aspects the focal point serves to give this flower a unique take.  <br/>Can''t be too critical it''s a lovely shot.  If I had a personal dislike/criticism it would only be to desaturate the yellow a little bit.  <br/>Congrats on a great image!</td>', 'Greetings from the CC!Very nice job, no distracting elements, good light and colors. What I like most is your choice of composition is good but my favorite is what you chose as the '' most in focus''  this is not the typical focal point but with all the other very well chosen aspects the focal point serves to give this flower a unique take.  Can''t be too critical it''s a lovely shot.  If I had a personal dislike/criticism it would only be to desaturate the yellow a little bit.  Congrats on a great image!', '2006-07-16 01:46:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2626027, 357312, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC. <br/>This shot to me is very well done overall, I like the light on the yeollw, and the DOF is great that you can see the other flowers.  The black really helps the yellow to pop.  The compostion is also good I think, yet something overall is not working, I think it may be the orange background.  I would like to see some maybe with all black?  Actually I think it is the combo of the black and the orange you have 2 backgrounds and a strong flower and even tho they all work individually I think my eye is not sure where to land. And the quality of the light seems different in each part.  All the elements are really well done, but together they are competing.  I hope that helps.  I think you are extremely close to a really great image.  <br/>Well done, congrats on a well placed image!</td>', 'Greetings from the CC. This shot to me is very well done overall, I like the light on the yeollw, and the DOF is great that you can see the other flowers.  The black really helps the yellow to pop.  The compostion is also good I think, yet something overall is not working, I think it may be the orange background.  I would like to see some maybe with all black?  Actually I think it is the combo of the black and the orange you have 2 backgrounds and a strong flower and even tho they all work individually I think my eye is not sure where to land. And the quality of the light seems different in each part.  All the elements are really well done, but together they are competing.  I hope that helps.  I think you are extremely close to a really great image.  Well done, congrats on a well placed image!', '2006-07-16 01:53:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2626078, 356123, 48228, '<td valign="top">This is just awesome Joey, and love it so very much, especially the "eerie dark mood" of the image..... So your "style" here, and add this one into my favorites, as it is just magical..... I have always appriciate your style of work, even though most are a little to dark for me, but this one, is perfect.</td>', 'This is just awesome Joey, and love it so very much, especially the "eerie dark mood" of the image..... So your "style" here, and add this one into my favorites, as it is just magical..... I have always appriciate your style of work, even though most are a little to dark for me, but this one, is perfect.', '2006-07-16 02:17:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2626099, 355839, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC. I see this is your very first entry, and you didn''t do too badly for your first try!  <br/> <br/>I was taken at once with the very,very nice background for this sunflower.  The vertical out-of-focus foliage in the background is original and captivating.  <br/> <br/>Because this was an advanced editing Challenge, my primary suggestion would be to edit out that little bit of flower at the lower right corner.  <br/> <br/>Second, I''d suggest a little groundskeeping here, to move that forward out-of-focus bud out of the way before the image was taken.  This would give a clear view to your center of attraction, that lovely sunflower in the middle.  If you keep a clothspin or the like in your camera bag you can move unwanted stuff out of the way and not harm anything.  Just a little thought for you...  <br/> <br/>But mostly I want to compliment you on a delicate, nice image that you obviously gave a lot of thought to making. <br/> <br/>Some of your commentors suggested you try to use the full 640 pixels allowed.  If you''re unsure how to resize for DPC, I think there is a tutorial that gives some good clues.  Look under tutorials to find it. <br/> <br/>Keep up the good work and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your photography.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Welcome to DPC. I see this is your very first entry, and you didn''t do too badly for your first try!   I was taken at once with the very,very nice background for this sunflower.  The vertical out-of-focus foliage in the background is original and captivating.   Because this was an advanced editing Challenge, my primary suggestion would be to edit out that little bit of flower at the lower right corner.   Second, I''d suggest a little groundskeeping here, to move that forward out-of-focus bud out of the way before the image was taken.  This would give a clear view to your center of attraction, that lovely sunflower in the middle.  If you keep a clothspin or the like in your camera bag you can move unwanted stuff out of the way and not harm anything.  Just a little thought for you...   But mostly I want to compliment you on a delicate, nice image that you obviously gave a lot of thought to making.  Some of your commentors suggested you try to use the full 640 pixels allowed.  If you''re unsure how to resize for DPC, I think there is a tutorial that gives some good clues.  Look under tutorials to find it.  Keep up the good work and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your photography.', '2006-07-16 02:28:18.000000', NULL, 0),
