(2688266, 354817, 50641, '<td valign="top">I thought this was wonderful, got an 8 from me. Very good sharpness level. Good tonal depth too. The only thing I wonder about is the orientation/composition - I wasn''t sure I liked the cuts on the top and bottom. If it were mine, I might experiment with making the crop more symmetrical or else maybe rotate the image so that the chops are at diagonals...?   Just musing :)</td>', 'I thought this was wonderful, got an 8 from me. Very good sharpness level. Good tonal depth too. The only thing I wonder about is the orientation/composition - I wasn''t sure I liked the cuts on the top and bottom. If it were mine, I might experiment with making the crop more symmetrical or else maybe rotate the image so that the chops are at diagonals...?   Just musing :)', '2006-08-02 12:41:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2692058, 354817, 40376, '<td valign="top">Almost surreal-like texture.<br/>But I like this photo a lot.<br/>Great B+W and great focus and framing.</td>', 'Almost surreal-like texture.But I like this photo a lot.Great B+W and great focus and framing.', '2006-08-03 12:43:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2692069, 355620, 40355, '<td valign="top">What might have worked better for you here would be to not totally desaturate the whole image, but to leave a wash of color.  Maybe set the saturation slider at -65ish, and then mask out the single flower, as you did, and boost it back up to full, or even a more than full (+25ish?).</td>', 'What might have worked better for you here would be to not totally desaturate the whole image, but to leave a wash of color.  Maybe set the saturation slider at -65ish, and then mask out the single flower, as you did, and boost it back up to full, or even a more than full (+25ish?).', '2006-08-03 12:45:50.000000', NULL, 0),
